{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-symbolic-character-table","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:symbolic-character-table","kind":"proposition","title":"Symbolic character table $\\chi_\\lambda(\\sigma)$ for all partitions $H_2$--$H_7$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-wedderburn-trace-identity"],"tags":["character","seminormal","symbolic","partition","self-conjugate"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.symbolic_character_table","text":"symbolic-character-table.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:symbolic-character-table\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Symbolic character table <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_\\lambda(\\sigma)</code> for all partitions <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2</code>--<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_7</code></em></p>\n<p><em>For every partition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\leq 7</code>, the single-generator\ncharacter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_\\lambda(\\sigma)</code> is a rational function of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>\nexpressible as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_\\lambda \\cdot h</code> where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h = q - q^{-1}</code> and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_\\lambda \\in \\mathbb{Q}(q^2)</code>.</em></p>\n<p><em>Self-conjugate partitions have integer coefficients:</em></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Partition</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi(\\sigma)/h</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2,1]</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">standard rep</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[3,1,1]</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">H<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">_{5}</code> Wigner</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[3,2,1]</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">H<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">_{6}</code> dominant (36% Plancherel)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[4,1,1,1]</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">10</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">H<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">_{7}</code> self-conjugate</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><em>Pair characters (exact in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>):</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\chi_{[3,1,1]}(\\sigma_i \\sigma_{i+1}) = h^2 = (q-q^{-1})^2</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\chi_{[3,1,1]}(\\sigma_i \\sigma_j)_{|i-j|\\geq 2} = h^2 - 2</code></pre>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\chi_{[3,1,1]}(\\sigma_i \\sigma_{i+1} \\sigma_{i+2}) = -h</code></pre>\n<p><em>Computed via seminormal form: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a_\\rho = h/(1-q^{-2\\rho})</code>\nsummed over standard Young tableaux.</em> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n"}
